  planner_response {
    response: "I have successfully created a clone of the **TripIt** travel organizer application using Material UI and Next.js.\n\n### Key Features Implemented:\n*   **TripIt Branding**: A custom Material UI theme was crafted to match TripIt\'s signature blue and orange color palette, along with its clean typographic style.\n*   **Trips Dashboard**:\n    *   **Tabbed Navigation**: Switch between \"Your Upcoming Trips,\" \"Others\' Upcoming Trips,\" and \"Past Trips.\"\n    *   **Trip Cards**: Detailed cards showing trip titles, dates, durations, and sharing status, complete with placeholder imagery.\n    *   **Quick Actions**: Buttons for \"Add a Trip\" and filtering by trip ownership.\n*   **Detailed Itinerary View**:\n    *   **Interactive Timeline**: A vertical timeline that organizes travel plans by date and time.\n    *   **Activity Icons**: Specific icons for flights and car rentals to make the itinerary scannable.\n    *   **Plan Details**: Displays flight numbers, terminals, addresses, and confirmation codes.\n    *   **Floating \"Add a Plan\" Button**: Matches the TripIt mobile/web experience for easy itinerary updates.\n*   **Smooth Transitions**: Integrated `motion/react` (Framer Motion) for fluid animations when navigating between the trips list and specific trip details.\n\n### Technical Details:\n*   **Framework**: Next.js 15 (App Router)\n*   **UI Library**: Material UI (MUI)\n*   **Icons**: Lucide React and MUI Icons\n*   **Animations**: Motion (formerly Framer Motion)\n*   **Styling**: Tailwind CSS for layout structure combined with MUI\'s powerful component system.\n\nYou can now view your upcoming trips, click on a trip card to see the full itinerary, and navigate back to the main dashboard."
    modified_response: "I have successfully created a clone of the **TripIt** travel organizer application using Material UI and Next.js.\n\n### Key Features Implemented:\n*   **TripIt Branding**: A custom Material UI theme was crafted to match TripIt\'s signature blue and orange color palette, along with its clean typographic style.\n*   **Trips Dashboard**:\n    *   **Tabbed Navigation**: Switch between \"Your Upcoming Trips,\" \"Others\' Upcoming Trips,\" and \"Past Trips.\"\n    *   **Trip Cards**: Detailed cards showing trip titles, dates, durations, and sharing status, complete with placeholder imagery.\n    *   **Quick Actions**: Buttons for \"Add a Trip\" and filtering by trip ownership.\n*   **Detailed Itinerary View**:\n    *   **Interactive Timeline**: A vertical timeline that organizes travel plans by date and time.\n    *   **Activity Icons**: Specific icons for flights and car rentals to make the itinerary scannable.\n    *   **Plan Details**: Displays flight numbers, terminals, addresses, and confirmation codes.\n    *   **Floating \"Add a Plan\" Button**: Matches the TripIt mobile/web experience for easy itinerary updates.\n*   **Smooth Transitions**: Integrated `motion/react` (Framer Motion) for fluid animations when navigating between the trips list and specific trip details.\n\n### Technical Details:\n*   **Framework**: Next.js 15 (App Router)\n*   **UI Library**: Material UI (MUI)\n*   **Icons**: Lucide React and MUI Icons\n*   **Animations**: Motion (formerly Framer Motion)\n*   **Styling**: Tailwind CSS for layout structure combined with MUI\'s powerful component system.\n\nYou can now view your upcoming trips, click on a trip card to see the full itinerary, and navigate back to the main dashboard."
